---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ExternalLink from '../components/ExternalLink.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import TickList from '../components/TickList.astro';
import Value from '../components/Value.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility"
  description="How the Pholoso Afrika Foundation website is built to be accessible and comfortable, how to use the Comfort & access settings, and how to report a problem."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Accessibility"
    title="Accessibility statement"
    lead="We want this website to be comfortable and easy to use for everyone, including neurodivergent people."
  />

  <Section narrow>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What we have done</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to meet the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines (WCAG) 2.2 at level AA. We also
        follow guidance on designing for neurodivergent and autistic people.
      </p>
      <TickList
        items={[
          'No animation, autoplay, pop-ups or moving content.',
          'Plain language, short sentences and clear headings.',
          'Large, readable text in the Atkinson Hyperlegible typeface.',
          'Links are always underlined. Links to other websites are marked with an arrow and open in the same tab.',
          'Every page and form works without JavaScript.',
          'Forms have visible labels, explain mistakes clearly and have no time limits.',
          'The same menu, footer and help links on every page.',
        ]}
      />

      <h2 id="comfort">Comfort & access settings</h2>
      <p>
        Choose the "Comfort & access" button at the bottom right of any page to change how the site
        looks and behaves. Your choices are saved only in your own browser, on this device.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Quick start:</strong> one-tap presets for feeling overwhelmed, finding reading
          hard, or not seeing clearly.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Colours:</strong> Standard, Calm (softer and muted), High contrast, or Dim
          (darker, for light sensitivity).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Text size:</strong> 100%, 115%, 130% or 150%.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reading spacing:</strong> more space between lines, letters and words.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reading guide:</strong> a band that helps you keep your place.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reduce motion</strong>, <strong>Simplified page</strong> and{' '}
          <strong>Hide images</strong>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Identity-first wording</strong> (see below).
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Reset all settings</strong> returns everything to normal.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>The settings need JavaScript. Without it, the website still works in its standard form.</p>

      <h2 id="wording">Why you can change the wording</h2>
      <p>
        Some people prefer person-first language, such as "child with autism". Others prefer
        identity-first language, such as "autistic child". We use person-first language by default
        and respect each person's choice. Turn on "Identity-first wording" to switch these phrases
        across the website.
      </p>

      <h2>Your own browser and device settings</h2>
      <p>
        We respect the settings on your device. If your device asks for less motion, more contrast
        or a dark theme, the website starts in the matching mode. Browser zoom up to 400% and
        Windows high contrast mode are supported. "Listen" buttons use your browser's built-in voice
        and only appear if your browser can read aloud.
      </p>

      <h2>Report a problem</h2>
      <p>
        If something on this website is hard to use, please tell us. Email{' '}
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and tell us which page and what went
        wrong. We will reply <Value value={site.accessibility.responseTime} />.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can read the guidance we follow:{' '}
        <ExternalLink href="https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/">WCAG 2.2</ExternalLink> and{' '}
        <ExternalLink href="https://www.w3.org/TR/coga-usable/">
          Making content usable for people with cognitive and learning disabilities
        </ExternalLink>
        .
      </p>
      <p>This statement was last reviewed on {site.accessibility.lastReviewed}.</p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
